## 3. the gate still bites on a tarball built without the exclusion list

The good tarball was saved, then the archive was rebuilt from an unfiltered
`git ls-files` list and the audit was run against it:

$ tar -tzf dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz | wc -l
90
$ mkdir -p /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/neg2
$ cp dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/neg2/good.tar.gz
$ git ls-files -z > /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/neg2/all.z
$ tar -C . -czf dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz \
      --transform='s|^|sm750hdmifb-0.6.0/|' --null -T /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/neg2/all.z
$ ./tests/audit-release.sh
Source archive contains development-only content: docs/plan
# exit: 1
$ cp /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/neg2/good.tar.gz dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz
$ ./tests/audit-release.sh
Release audit passed: /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/tree/dist/RELEASE-AUDIT.txt
# exit: 0

## 4. one edit at the shared list moves both the packager and the gate

`docs/specs` was appended to `sm750_dev_only` in packaging/source-excludes.sh,
the archive was rebuilt and the audit was run:

$ ./build-package.sh >/dev/null && ./tests/audit-release.sh
Release audit passed: /mega/tmp/sm750/t18/tree/dist/RELEASE-AUDIT.txt
# exit: 0
$ tar -tzf dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz | grep -c 'docs/specs/'
0

The entry was then removed and the file restored. The reverse direction is
asserted by the suite, in both directions:

$ # docs/plan deleted from sm750_dev_only
$ ./tests/check-drm-packaging.sh
# exit: 1   (the `grep -F 'docs/plan' "$excludes"` assertion at
#            tests/check-drm-packaging.sh:37 fails)
$ # docs/plan restored
$ ./tests/check-drm-packaging.sh
Unified DRM package checks passed
# exit: 0

So a development-only path cannot be dropped from the shared list, and it
cannot be hard-coded back into a consumer either: tests/check-drm-packaging.sh:45-49
fails if `:(exclude)docs/` appears in build-package.sh or tests/audit-release.sh.

## 5. the non-git fallback branch excludes the same list

A copy of the tree without .git was packaged from the fallback branch:

$ ./build-package.sh
/mega/tmp/sm750/t18/nogit/dist/sm750hdmifb_0.6.0_all.deb
/mega/tmp/sm750/t18/nogit/dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz
/mega/tmp/sm750/t18/nogit/dist/SHA256SUMS
# exit: 0
$ tar -tzf dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz | wc -l
104
$ tar -tzf dist/sm750hdmifb-0.6.0-source.tar.gz |
      grep -c '^sm750hdmifb-0.6.0/docs/\(plan\|evidence\|images\)/'
0

104 rather than 90 because the copy carries the untracked working-tree files,
which the fallback branch cannot distinguish from tracked ones by design.

